Subject: [PATCH 08020/11362] [outer-loop] The guard prompt omitted the two
 classes about writing to tracked state, so guards were never asked

Applies eight review findings to the Layer-2 / Layer-3 work shipped earlier
today. Three were code defects in the deliverable itself, and two of those are
the same bug class the deliverable exists to hunt -- recorded rather than
quietly fixed, because a discipline that commits its own bug class and hides it
is worth less than one that shows the failure mode is easy.

WHAT THE AUDIT WOULD HAVE CAUGHT
- The origin incident, in an acceptance test against the real pre-widening lint
  recovered from 7ba6dd7d6: SILENT_NON_FIRING, 2/2 runs, one naming
  `inference_substrate_correction_note` verbatim and quoting the line that let
  it through. It also found five further real gaps in that lint, unprompted:
  fail-open on git failure, and --diff-filter=M excluding added/deleted/renamed
  artifacts.
- Class D and E questions now actually reach guards. They did not before: this
  commit's first finding is that PER_GUARD_PROMPT -- used by the ONLY targets
  that are themselves guards -- spliced none of SHARED_BUG_CLASSES, under a
  comment claiming it was "shared by every prompt in this file". Proven, not
  theorised: a fixture writing into results/ on every run drew eight findings
  from that prompt and not one mentioned the write.

WHAT IT STILL WOULD NOT CATCH
- Anything, for ~7 milestone-closes, on the surface added because of a live
  incident. The offset was persisted at 45 of 168 units while the ten new guard
  targets sat at indices 0-9, and the conductor runs --limit 20. Ordering the
  guards first did nothing; the docstring asserting otherwise was simply wrong.
  Fixed with a units_signature that discards a stale offset. Note what this
  means: for most of today the extension was real code that would not have run.
- A test-driven rewrite of README.md. Observed live during review and NOT fixed
  here: operator_curated_docs_lint.py is a commit-msg hook that only refuses
  subjects starting with [conductor], and every recent commit is [outer-loop].
  It exited 0 on a gutted README. That is an operator call on widening the lint
  or making the runtime guard fail rather than warn; this commit's contribution
  is that the guard is now audited surface and reachable at the next run.
- A prompt-level claim that a reviewer disagrees with. Coverage is enforced by
  marker presence, not by whether the reviewer answers the question well.

CODE
- PER_GUARD_PROMPT gains class E and class D's write-target framing; BUG_CLASS_
  MARKERS + a test assert every prompt covers every class, driven off the tuple
  so a sixth class cannot be added without wiring it everywhere.
- Rotation: units_signature (count + label hash, NOT bodies -- editing a
  function must not discard progress) and resolve_rotation_offset, extracted so
  it is tested rather than reimplemented in the test file.
- exists_in_repo narrowed .exists() -> .is_file() + a suffix allow-list, so a
  bare `scripts/` no longer un-voids a flagged verdict.
- --check-targets wired as the qa-layer-audit-scope-check pre-commit hook. It
  shipped with no caller, which is trust-without-verification one level up from
  what it was written to defeat.

CONTRACT
- Rule 3 enumerated 8 of the 16 OPERATOR_CURATED_PATHS and called it "the
  protected set" -- the same pattern-narrower-than-concept bug, in the contract
  that defines the concept. Now points at the tuple as single source of truth.
- Operator step 2 said `git checkout --` the reported paths. Under concurrent
  workflows --check output is a SUPERSET (the snapshot baseline is shared
  mutable state); it reported ~75 paths here, mostly another agent's
  uncommitted migration. Executing it literally is the data-loss class "Never
  Stash" exists to prevent. Now says so.
- The 139/99 and 1,696/704 counts are marked historical; the paths.py migration
  is driving the first toward zero and a later reader would have read a lower
  number as the rule being wrong.

SPEC
Adds REQ-ARC-WMTE-6042 (sibling of 6041: 6041 is the record being rewritten, 6042
is the DETECTION layer's blind spots) with six scenarios, and retires this test
file's "Spec refs: none" declaration, which was true when it only covered chunk
extraction and is not now.

VERIFICATION
51/51 mutations killed across both suites (17 new + 34 phase-1). Two of the new
tests survived their first mutation run and were rewritten to bite; one phase-1
mutation regressed because the suffix allow-list made the path-escape check
decorative, which turned out to be more interesting than the mutation --
`..` is unreachable for a leading-dot path because .strip() eats the dots, so
the rule only earns its place on an interior traversal, and the test now uses
one. 79 tests pass, ruff clean, --check-targets OK, canonical-url-lint OK.
CLAUDE.md is append-and-annotate only: +433/-1, the single deletion being an
in-place annotation with every word preserved.

Staged by explicit path, not `git add -A`: 83 files in the tree belong to a
concurrent migration workflow and are deliberately untouched.

